{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED AND PUSHED as Gerrit change 2623 -- https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2623 -- awaiting LLM-Review and Verified. Not closed.\n\nPLAN REVIEW CAUGHT A REAL DESIGN ERROR ON THE THIRD PASS, and it is worth recording because the plan\nread plausibly with a mechanism that does not exist: '--keep-storage' is a 'docker builder prune'\n(BuildKit) flag and CANNOT bound the image store. So the planned '15 GiB image/layer share' had NO\nENFORCEMENT MECHANISM AT ALL. Rewritten around retention instead. (Pass two returned INDETERMINATE\nfrom an LLM-provider tool failure -- DDGSException, infrastructure rather than the plan; every\ndeterministic criterion passed.) Fourth pass certified at verified_at_sha 3ae5c7a6082c.\n\nTHE CRUX -- seeing bytes 'docker system df' cannot: observability.sh section 2f takes TWO INDEPENDENT\nMEASUREMENTS OF THE SAME BYTES and publishes their difference.\n  filesystem truth: bounded 'du -sx' over /var/lib/docker and over overlay2 (-x will not cross into a\n    mounted overlay2/*/merged; one du run counts a hardlinked file once)\n  daemon ledger: docker system df Images + Containers + Build Cache, human sizes parsed to bytes\n    (SI and binary suffixes; Local Volumes excluded -- they are not in overlay2)\n  docker_unaccounted_bytes = overlay2 truth - ledger, clamped at 0\nA test REPLAYS THE INCIDENT EXACTLY: 16 GiB overlay2 against a 9.529GB ledger yields ~6.6 GiB of\nresidue. Every reading is gated on its own measurement succeeding, so a failed probe publishes\nNOTHING and treat_missing_data=breaching pages -- rather than fabricating a 0 that would read as an\nempty Docker root. That is the bff5 dead-man lesson applied correctly on the first attempt.\n\nTHE MOST IMPORTANT HONESTY IN THIS CHANGE, written into the code rather than glossed: the budget has\nTHREE UNEQUAL ENFORCEMENT STRENGTHS. BuildKit is genuinely capped by the daemon's own builder.gc; the\nimage/layer share is held only by RETENTION, because Docker has no image-store ceiling; and orphaned\noverlay2 is bounded by NOTHING and is alarm-only. A reader who assumes 'capped' means the same thing\nin all three places would be wrong, and the code now says so.\n\nTHREE ALARMS, because none implies another (the 3e92 argument): the whole budget; the BuildKit\nGENERATOR at its own share (100% of a 5 GiB share is invisible inside a 20 GiB budget reading 60%,\nand a runaway image set saturates the budget while BuildKit sits at 10%); and unaccounted overlay2 --\nthe first two say HOW FULL, only the third says FULL OF WHAT PRUNE STRUCTURALLY CANNOT TOUCH, which\nchanges remediation from 'prune harder' (measured at ~1.06 GB against 29 GB) to a daemon-level\nreclaim. All 300/3/2, breaching, SNS on both edges, pinned by name with floors raised 21->24, 16->19,\n15->18.\n\nRED-first: 31 failed / 4 passed before implementation, and the 4 passes were the 'publishes nothing'\nnegatives that only became meaningful once the metrics existed -- correctly identified as vacuous\nrather than counted as coverage.\n\nVerification: make lint 0; make typecheck clean (755 files); terraform fmt -check 0 and validate\nSuccess; mechanism new=0 (no marker needed -- the detectors do not scan infra/); complexity new=0;\napi-surface and predates-gate-guard-parity pass after git add; FULL SUITE on a frozen tree 19316\npassed, 63 skipped, 0 failures in 26m16s. NO TERRAFORM APPLIED -- fmt -check and\ninit -backend=false + validate only.\n\nCARRY-OVER FIXED IN PASSING, which the ADR flags as an obligation with no owning story:\nrebar-root-disk-pressure's description still said '30G ROOT disk' against a 60 GiB volume, and now\npoints readers at the per-generator alarms before they reach for du.\n\nNOTES LEFT FOR THE SIBLING STORIES, deliberately not acted on:\n - compose-up.sh has no reusable 'run a host-config installer' seam; there are now five independent\n   'if ! bash ...; then echo WARN; fi' blocks and S3/S4/S5 will each add a sixth, seventh, eighth. An\n   install_or_warn helper would collapse them, but that refactors everyone's lines.\n - observability.sh is now 974 lines and each story adds a section 2x, re-spelling the\n   put-metric-data + logger pair. Worth extracting a shared 'publish a gauge if measurable' helper\n   once S3-S5 land, not before.\n - S5 SHOULD EXTEND docker-storage-cap.sh's budget rather than add a second one: ADR 0112 is explicit\n   that writable container layers are a sub-share of the same /var/lib/docker budget, and\n   DOCKER_IMAGE_SHARE_BYTES is already exported from --print-env for exactly that.\n\nPre-existing failure identified and NOT mine: test_mechanism_delta.py::\ntest_a_marker_in_a_new_gate_scripts_head_admits_it fails with ModuleNotFoundError when run ALONE on\nthis host, fails identically at pristine origin/main in a throwaway worktree, and passes inside the\nfull-suite run -- a sys.path artifact of single-file invocation."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788536440509040001,"uuid":"efae787b-6ef5-4ef1-b50c-c987ff21b5f1"}